{
  "_comment": "The characters of CardBrix the game (a cleaned version of the design brief cardbrix_characters_config.json). Read by the client (client/src/lib/game/characters.js), by the server (src/services/avatarConfig.js) and by scripts/build-game-skins.js. A character is playable only once its sheet is built (its id is then in avatarSpec.json `looks`, written by the build script). No prices, rarities or accessories: characters are free and what they hold is drawn into the sheet. Names and region labels are translated in the locale files (game.characters.*, game.classes.*, game.creator.regions.*). `regions` maps each colour part of the avatar to null (not recolourable for this character) or { label, ref, band }: `ref` are reference colours of that zone as drawn (a hex, or { hex, band } for a colour found only at some height) (the build script assigns each pixel to the zone with the closest reference colour), `band` the part of the body height (0 = top of the head, 1 = soles) where the zone can be, to tell apart zones with similar colours.",
